hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2686","Narrated to us Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari with an unusual report: Narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Muhammad — meaning ibn Ishaq — narrated to me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn 'Umar used to do that — meaning he used to cut the socks (khuffayn) for women — until Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd informed him, on the authority of 'A'ishah, that:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted a concession to women regarding the socks (khuffayn).\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
